<BaseLayout title="About The Latent Playbook">
  <article class="space-y-8 text-text/90">
    <h1 class="font-heading text-4xl leading-tight text-text">About The Latent Playbook</h1>
    <p>
      We stand at a pivotal moment where the craft of filmmaking is being fundamentally reimagined by artificial
      intelligence. The line between director, animator, and technologist is blurring, opening up a universe of creative
      possibilities. The Latent Playbook was created to navigate this new terrain, serving as a guide for
      creators in this emerging field.
    </p>
    <p>
      Born from research and experimentation at <a href="https://sites.google.com/nyu.edu/hypercinemalab/home" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NYU's Hypercinema Lab</a>, this project is not a rigid instruction manual, but
    a dynamic playbook designed for hands-on creation. It is a practical resource for anyone interested in the
    burgeoning field of generative cinema, prioritizing the power and accessibility of open-source
    text-to-image and text-to-video models, but not limited to them.
    </p>
    <p>
      The playbook aims to empower filmmakers, artists, and technologists to experiment with AI-driven tools and
      techniques, fostering a community of practice around generative media. By sharing our findings, workflows, and
      reflections, we hope to contribute to the collective understanding of how AI can augment human creativity in the
      realm of moving images.
    </p>
    <h2>What You'll Find Inside</h2>
    <p>
      The playbook is broken down into a series of "plays," each one tackling a specific creative challenge or use case
      in AI filmmaking. From learning how to generate a consistent character across multiple scenes, to using a person's
      real-world motion to drive a digital avatar, each play may include:
    </p>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-text/85">
      <li><strong>Tools:</strong> A breakdown of the primary software and models used, with an emphasis on open-source solutions.</li>
      <li><strong>Advice:</strong> Practical tips and best practices discovered through experimentation—what works, what doesn't, and why.</li>
      <li><strong>Resources:</strong> A curated list of links to essential papers, tutorials, and communities to help you learn more.</li>
      <li><strong>Examples:</strong> Sample output clips (videos and GIFs) that demonstrate the potential of each technique.</li>
      <li><strong>Reflections:</strong> Thoughts on the value, process and impact of AI on filmmaking.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Playbook Editors</h2>
    <p><a href="https://www.ygzhang.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Yuguang (YG) Zhang</a></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
